# gateway cannot vet, so its CREATE is rejected. The helper is re-seeded directly
# per test (postgis_preseed.sql, applied by the patched run_test.pl); where its
# signature would collide with another file's overload it is renamed per file
# (patchPostGISConflictingHelpers) so seeding stays unambiguous. Only the rejected
# CREATE remains, plus any "at character N" cursor-offset shifts on geometry
# messages.
--- a
+++ b
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 max|node|22
 max|edge|26
+ERROR: EXECUTE of a runtime-built statement inside a PL/pgSQL body is not supported: the statement text is not a constant, so it cannot be checked for unsafe session-state changes
